# Partners

Who this client never writes competitively about.

**Why this file is a file and not a sentence in BRAND.md.** A prose honesty rule does not
stop an agent writing "alternatives to X" about a partner. The agent is optimising for a
SERP, and the rule is a line in a document it read once. This file is parsed by
`voice_check.py` and by `serp_gate.py`, so the rule has an exit code behind it.

On one account this blocked whole article types, and three partners turned up ranking on
target SERPs inside a single week.

## Format

One partner per `## heading`. The heading text is the name the gates match on, so use the
name as it appears in copy and in domains. Everything under the heading is for the writer.

- `voice_check.py` blocks "alternatives to <partner>", "<partner> competitors",
  "<brand> vs <partner>" and "best <partner> ..." anywhere in a draft.
- `serp_gate.py` rejects a keyword whose live SERP has a partner ranking on it.

---

## Example Partner Inc

- **Relationship:** what they actually are to this client (supplier, integration, investor,
  reseller). One line.
- **How they may appear in copy:** the only framings that are allowed. Be specific, because
  "positively" is not a rule a writer can apply.
- **Never:** the framings that are banned, named explicitly.
- **Domains:** partnerinc.com, docs.partnerinc.com

